  "summary": "The elegant, minimalist staging aesthetic of Kunqu opera, China's oldest continuously performed theatrical form.",
  "description": "Kunqu features spare, poetic settings with simple props and gestures that suggest rather than represent, using subtle movements and poetic language to convey complex emotions. This refined aesthetic developed during the Ming Dynasty as a reaction against the more elaborate forms of opera, emphasizing literary quality and emotional subtlety through minimalist staging.",
